course: dictionary
lesson: 14119
title: Microbial: tiny living things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Microbes are tiny living things, like bacteria, fungi and some algae. Most are too small to see without a microscope. Microbial is the describing word: it means to do with microbes.
explain: The word can also mean caused by microbes. «A microbial infection» is an illness caused by tiny living things. In «antimicrobial» soap, the word anti means against, so the soap works against microbes.
explain: Context helps you here. «Scientists looked at the microbial life in a drop of pond water.» The words microscope and pond water tell you that microbial life means living things too small to see with your eyes alone.
fact: Microbial is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like «microbial life» or «a microbial infection».
fact: Microbes are tiny living things, such as bacteria, fungi and some algae.
fact: «Microbial growth» on old food is a warning that the food may not be safe to eat.
fact: Some microbes are helpful: they help make yogurt, bread and compost.
fact: Handwashing helps to reduce the microbial spread of illness.
exercise: «Scientists looked at the microbial life in a drop of pond water.» What does microbial mean here? | To do with very cold weather | *To do with tiny living things | To do with big animals like cows | To do with rocks and stones
exercise: «The child had a microbial infection and stayed in bed.» Find and copy the word that describes the infection. | stayed | infection | *microbial | child
exercise: Why are microbes not always bad? | They are only found in space | They always make us ill | They are all large animals | *Some help us, like making yogurt and bread
test: «Handwashing reduces microbial spread.» What does this mean? | The water gets hotter when we wash | The sink stops working | *Fewer microbes spread from place to place | More soap is used up
test: What is a microbe? | A large animal kept on a farm | *A tiny living thing, like bacteria | A type of rock found in the hills | A piece of metal used in building
exam: «The soap is antimicrobial.» What does this tell you about the soap? | It turns the soap into a liquid | *It works against microbes | It is made from old bread | It makes the soap smell sweet
